0001                  /* SNES machine glue: host hooks + run loop. Boots UNIX v6 single-user.
0002                   *
0003                   * Memory map (measured, see docs/M3-notes.md):
0004                   *   guest 128 KB  -> cart SRAM banks $20-$2F (bus.c PDP11_RAM_SRAM)
0005                   *   v6 root image -> cart ROM at $D00000 (raw2sfc --at 0x100000), RO + overlay
0006                   *   rk1 swap      -> 62 KB WRAM buffer, bank $7F (bus.c PDP11_DISK_ROM;
0007                   *                    the SPC700/APU-RAM version replaces that buffer later)
0008                   *   console       -> Mode 5 64x28 (console.c)
0009                   *
0010                   * Mailbox for the Mesen Lua harness (low WRAM, reserved in linker.scm):
0011                   *   $0100 magic: 0xB007 running, 0xDEAD host panic
0012                   *   $0102/$0104 guest icount lo/hi   $0106 output count
0013                   *   $0108/$010A 24-bit address of the 1 KB output transcript ring
0014                   *
0015                   * Boot input is canned: "unix\r" at the '@' prompt; switch register 0173030
0016                   * makes v6 init go single-user (no login). When the first '#' prompt appears
0017                   * we type a small demo. Real keyboard input is a later milestone.
0018                   */
